  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pre-feasibility Scoping Sustainable Territorial Development of Kaback, Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Recent dike breakthroughs in Kaback, Guinee, led to an emergency. Floods have worsened living conditions for local farmers and fishermen. The great agricultural potential of Kaback has been left unused and continues to decline because of residents migrating elsewhere and structural damage to the physical system and drinking water provision.A Dutch Risk Reduction mission has delivered advice for both short-term and long-term measures. The current scoping will lay the foundation for the implementation of no-regret measures and will lay the foundation for sustainable territorial development and land use planning of the Kaback region in Guinee through a commonly supported integrated Territorial Development Plan ready for implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
